  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 77f9e9cb1e7fc492e846f00b1dfb0259, type: 3}
  m_Name: Final
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueObject
  dialogue:
  - You might not want to venture forth...
  - A being by the name of Schopenhauer haunts these hills.
  - 'Once a great philospher, he has since lost himself. '
  - He believes suffering is a sign of resistance to the will of the world...
  - For this will to be complete, we must all be one.
  - He's taken to rather.....violent means to eliminate individuality.
  - Do you think humans fare better depending on one another or standing strong on
    their own?
  responses:
  - responseText: Together.
    dialogueObject: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 31072572588974ee5ae344c8910c7d3f, type: 2}
  - responseText: On their own.
    dialogueObject: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 31072572588974ee5ae344c8910c7d3f, type: 2}
